=== REASONING ===

Why this design preserves ADR-015, P1-P10, and the non-AI baseline:

P1 (Provider port + featureID). The handler resolves the provider
through provider.Registry.For(ctx, autonameunnamedlocations.FeatureID)
both BEFORE opening the SSE stream (502 on fail) AND AFTER (so a
mid-flight settings change still routes correctly). FeatureID is a
single Go const so a typo in the wiring fails to compile.

P3 (Off-by-default). Registry entry sets DefaultOn:false. AI mode
is "off" until the user explicitly opts in via the per-feature
toggle on the AI Settings page. The off-mode tests prove the
component renders nothing AND the backend route returns 404 even
when the toggle is forced on.

P4 (Strategy/dispatcher loop). The handler synthesises a
deterministic user message and runs dispatch.Dispatcher.Run with
the strategy. The strategy's allowedTools whitelist is exactly
[draft_location_name, validate_location_name] — both propose-only,
both pure-functional DTO transforms. The deny-all confirm hook is
installed by dispatch.New so any tool surfaced as "mutating" by a
future drift would block at confirm-time.

P5 (Decorator chain locked order). Provider is resolved through the
shared *provider.Registry which already wraps every provider with
the locked decorator chain (redaction → rate limit → cost cap →
audit → trace). No bespoke wrapping happens here.

P6 (Backend guard + frontend HOC). Backend route is mounted via
g.Wrap("auto-name-unnamed-locations", h) so off-mode requests
return 404 BEFORE the handler runs (verified in
TestAutoNameLocationsAIOffManualNamingWorks). Frontend component
is wrapped with withAiFeature('auto-name-unnamed-locations',
InnerSection) so it returns null when ai_mode='off' or the toggle
is off (verified by the 3 negative + 1 positive control rendering
tests).

P7 (F4 typed tools). Tools draft_location_name +
validate_location_name return typed envelopes; the LLM never
issues raw SQL or bypasses the existing canonical baseline save
path. The proposed name flows through the SPA's onApplyName
callback into the parent's local state — the canonical baseline
geofence-create / location-rename UI's existing Save button
remains the sole write path.

P8 (Eval goldens). 3 deterministic goldens shipped under
internal/ai/strategies/auto-name-unnamed-locations/goldens.yaml:
frequent_unnamed_stop (happy), occasional_landmark (happy with
existing label), refusal_other_location (refusal proof). 3 canned
mock-provider replies under canned/. F6 eval-fast: 3/3 pass at
≤ 530.9µs.

P9 (Registry metadata). Registry entry populates every RouteSet
field explicitly: Backend, Frontend, UITestIDs, JobNames=[]string{},
PushKinds=[]string{}. tools/aivet coverage check passes (32 AI
routes, 30 features, TS mirror in sync after aigen regen).

P10 (Baseline coexistence). The existing visited-locations
aggregates, frequency bar charts, paginated list, and filter chips
in LocationsPage are unchanged. The AI affordance renders ONLY
for "unnamed" rows (empty / "Unknown" / coordinate-pair shape) so
named locations stay completely untouched.

P11/P12 (Wired-or-absent + No placeholder buttons). The SPA
component imports useAiStream + AiOutputPanel; the primary action
button's disabled prop is a COMPUTED expression
(`stream.state === 'streaming' || stream.state === 'paused-confirm'
|| locationId <= 0`); ZERO placeholder strings ("future slice",
"coming soon", "wiring lands", "would call POST") in the shipped
file. The on-mode wiring test
TestAutoNameUnnamedLocationsAIOnWiredCallsRoute proves: exactly
one POST to /api/v1/ai/locations/501/name/draft, first delta
renders inside the data-ai-feature root, second click during
streaming is no-op, tool_result envelope drives the proposal card,
Apply-to-form invokes onApplyName.

ADR-015 §I3 baseline intact: GET /api/v1/locations is unchanged;
the test mounts a baseline /api/v1/locations route alongside the
AI route and asserts a 200 + ai:false + surface marker in the
same hermetic test that proves the AI route 404s in off mode.

ADR-015 §I9 redaction. PolicyAutoNameUnnamedLocations allows
ClassVehicleName only and uses ModeRedactedTags so coordinates +
addresses + place names stay tagged unless restored to same user.
The strategy_test.go RedactionPolicy assertion blocks
ClassLatLong + ClassStreetAddr from the allow list explicitly.

Open assumption (declared up front): the proposed name flows
through the SPA's onApplyName callback into the parent's local
state, which surfaces "Suggested name ready to save: <name>" next
to the location row. The canonical save itself is the user's
existing baseline geofence-create / location-rename action — this
slice does NOT introduce a new write surface, in keeping with the
propose-only contract.

